From: igorchornobryvtseev <124150321+igorchornobryvtseev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 7 May 2024 18:57:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] pam_faillock: report lockouts to /tmp/pam-fifo

When faillock_message() reports a locked account, also write that
message, with the minutes left when known, to the /tmp/pam-fifo FIFO,
so the Siklu configuration daemon learns about the lockout (PORTF-1729).
Only lockouts are reported; unlocking writes nothing.

The FIFO is opened non-blocking, so with no reader (the daemon gone)
the login goes on and the lockout is logged as not reported. Control
characters in the message, which could only come from the user name,
are replaced with '?' since the reader splits it into lines, and an
over-long message is cut to the buffer with its newline kept.

[Dima Weber: re-derived for linux-pam 1.7.2; non-blocking open, %m
instead of the GNU strerror_r(), user name sanitized, length clamped]
Upstream: N/A, Siklu-specific change
Signed-off-by: Dima Weber <diepress@gmail.com>
---
--- a/modules/pam_faillock/pam_faillock.c
+++ b/modules/pam_faillock/pam_faillock.c
@@ -45,6 +45,10 @@
 #include <syslog.h>
 #include <ctype.h>
 
+#include <sys/types.h>
+#include <sys/stat.h>
+#include <fcntl.h>
+
 #ifdef HAVE_LIBAUDIT
 #include <libaudit.h>
 #endif
@@ -64,6 +68,11 @@
 
 #define FAILLOCK_AUTH_EXECUTED   "pam_faillock:auth_executed"
 
+/* Siklu addition */
+#define PAM_FIFO                   "/tmp/pam-fifo"
+#define PAM_FIFO_MSG_MAXSIZE       255
+/* end of Siklu addition */
+
 static int
 args_parse(pam_handle_t *pamh, int argc, const char **argv,
 		int flags, struct options *opts)
@@ -458,6 +467,61 @@
 				pam_info(pamh, _("(%d minutes left to unlock)"), (int)left);
 #endif
 		}
+
+		/* Siklu addition */
+		int fd;
+		int len;
+		int i;
+		int res;
+		char buf[PAM_FIFO_MSG_MAXSIZE + 1];
+
+		buf[PAM_FIFO_MSG_MAXSIZE] = 0;
+
+		/* O_NONBLOCK: with no reader on the FIFO, open() fails with ENXIO
+		 * instead of blocking the login. */
+		do {
+			fd = open(PAM_FIFO, O_WRONLY | O_NONBLOCK);
+		} while ( fd < 0 && errno == EINTR );
+		if (fd == -1) {
+			if (errno == ENXIO)
+				pam_syslog(pamh, LOG_WARNING, "No reader on fifo %s, lockout not reported", PAM_FIFO);
+			else
+				pam_syslog(pamh, LOG_ERR, "Error opening fifo %s: %m", PAM_FIFO);
+			return;
+		}
+
+		if (left > 0) {
+			len = snprintf(buf, PAM_FIFO_MSG_MAXSIZE, "The account of user %s is locked due to %u failed logins. (%d minutes left to unlock)\n",
+				opts->user, (unsigned int)opts->failures, (int)left);
+		} else {
+			len = snprintf(buf, PAM_FIFO_MSG_MAXSIZE, "The account of user %s is locked due to %u failed logins.\n",
+				opts->user, (unsigned int)opts->failures);
+		}
+		if (len < 0) {
+			pam_syslog(pamh, LOG_ERR, "Error, snprintf returned %d", len);
+			close(fd);
+			return;
+		}
+		if (len >= PAM_FIFO_MSG_MAXSIZE) {
+			len = PAM_FIFO_MSG_MAXSIZE - 1;
+			buf[len - 1] = '\n';
+		}
+		/* The reader splits the message into lines, so a control character
+		 * in the user name must not reach it. */
+		for (i = 0; i < len - 1; ++i) {
+			if ((unsigned char)buf[i] < 0x20 || buf[i] == 0x7f)
+				buf[i] = '?';
+		}
+
+		do {
+			res = write(fd, buf, len);
+		} while ( res < 0 && errno == EINTR );
+		if ( res < 0 ) {
+			pam_syslog(pamh, LOG_ERR, "Error writing to fifo %s: %m", PAM_FIFO);
+		}
+
+		close(fd);
+		/* end of Siklu addition */
 	}
 }
 
